#DESCRIPTION
2-level AMR GEM-like Harris sheet, hybrid PIC: coarse-fine interface stability

A small Harris sheet with the GEM challenge parameters (Birn et al. 2001):
lambda0 = 0.5 d_i, nb = 0.2, Ti/Te = 5, B0 = 1, conducting y walls, code units
with d_i = v_A = 1/sqrt(4*pi) and Omega_ci = 1. The box is only 1.6 x 3.2 d_i
and the run is 30 steps long, so it is not a reconnection benchmark: it checks
that a refined patch with fine dx = 0.05 d_i (base 0.1 d_i) next to low-density
lobes stays stable. Injecting the fine E into the covered coarse nodes drove a
2*dx_coarse mode along the interface here; max |B| reached 3x B0 within 26
steps. validate.py checks the coarse-fine interface
diagnostics (divB-AMR) and that max |B| stays near its initial value.

#INITFROMSWMF
F                       initFromSWMF

#GEOMETRY
-0.22568                xMin  [Lx = 1.6 d_i]
 0.22568                xMax
-0.45135                yMin  [Ly = 3.2 d_i]
 0.45135                yMax
-0.5                    zMin  [thin invariant direction, 1 cell]
 0.5                    zMax

#NCELL
16                      nCellX  [base dx = 0.1 d_i; level 1: 0.05 d_i]
32                      nCellY
1                       nCellZ

#MAXBLOCKSIZE
32                      maxBlockSizeX  [one block per level patch: small blocks multiply the
32                      maxBlockSizeY   coarse-fine fills, which dominate the cost here]
1                       maxBlockSizeZ

#PERIODICITY
T                       isPeriodicX
F                       isPeriodicY
T                       isPeriodicZ

#FIELDBOXBOUNDARY
periodic                fieldBoxBoundaryLo  (x)
periodic                fieldBoxBoundaryHi
conducting              fieldBoxBoundaryLo  (y; conducting walls matching GEM challenge)
conducting              fieldBoxBoundaryHi
periodic                fieldBoxBoundaryLo  (z)
periodic                fieldBoxBoundaryHi

#PARTICLEBOXBOUNDARY
periodic                particleBoxBoundaryLo
periodic                particleBoxBoundaryHi
reflect                 particleBoxBoundaryLo  (y; reflecting walls matching GEM challenge)
reflect                 particleBoxBoundaryHi
periodic                particleBoxBoundaryLo
periodic                particleBoxBoundaryHi

#FIELDSOLVER
hybrid

#RESISTIVITY
8.0e5                   etaResistivity  [m^2/s; small background resistivity]

#ELECTRONTEMPERATURE
0.6923                  electronTemperature  [eV; Te_code = 1/(48*pi) ~ 0.00663 code units, Ti/Te = 5]
1.0                     electronGamma        [isothermal fluid electrons]
65.15939                electronDensity0     [1/cc; n_e0 = 1.0 code units]

#SMOOTHMOMENTS
T                       doSmoothMoments [smooth ion moments to suppress particle shot noise]
3                       nSmoothMoments
0.5                     coefSmoothMoments

#MINIMUMDENSITY
0.1                     rhoMinOhm

#DIVB
F                       useHyperbolicCleaning
T                       alwaysComputeDivB

#FIELDSUBCYCLE
80                      nSubcycle      [whistler CFL at the level-1 dx = 0.05 d_i]
F                       isAutoSubcycle

#FIELDINTEGRATOR
rk4                     fieldIntegrator

#PLASMA
1                       nSpecies
1.0                     mass           Species 0: ions
1.0                     charge

#UNIFORMSTATE
13.03188                rho [/cc]   Species 0: ions (nb = 0.20 code units = 0.20 * 65.15939)
0.0                     ux [km/s]
0.0                     uy [km/s]
0.0                     uz [km/s]
40168.0                 T [K]          ion temperature (Ti_code = 5/(48*pi) ~ 0.03316, Ti/Te = 5)
0.0                     bx [T]
0.0                     by [T]
0.0                     bz [T]
0.0                     ex [V/m]
0.0                     ey [V/m]
0.0                     ez [V/m]

#TESTCASE
gem

#GEMIC
1.0                     b0       [asymptotic in-plane field B0 = 1.0]
0.5                     tp       [tp = 0.5 yields delta_n = 1.0, so n(0) = nb + n0 = 0.2 + 1.0 = 1.2]
0.14105                 lambda0  [current sheet half-width = 0.5 d_i = 0.5 / sqrt(4*pi) code units]
0.02821                 apert    [vector potential perturbation amplitude psi0 = 0.1 * B0 * d_i]
T                       useStandardGem
F                       useUniformPressure
T                       useUniformIonPressure  [stationary ions; electron fluid carries diamagnetic current]
0.2                     nb       [background density ratio nb = 0.2]
standard                pertType

#TIMESTEPPING
T                       useFixedDt
0.005                   dt       [Omega_ci^-1]

#NORMALIZATION
1.0e5                   lNormSI  [m; lNorm = 100 km]
1.0e5                   uNormSI  [m/s; uNorm = 100 km/s]

#MONITOR
5                       dnReport

#SAVELOG
10                      dnSavePic
100                     dnSavePT

#PARTICLES
3                       nParticle per cell in X
3                       nParticle per cell in Y
1                       nParticle per cell in Z

#SAVEPLOT
1                       nPlot
z=0 fluid ascii pic     plotString
-1                      dn
0.15                    dt
-1                      dx  [native AMR output]

The box |x| < 0.4 d_i, |y| < 1.2 d_i is refined 2x. Its y interfaces lie in the
lobes (n ~ 0.23), where the grid-scale mode grew in the full GEM deck.
#REGION
layer                   name
box                     shape
-0.11284                xMin  [|x| < 0.4 d_i]
 0.11284                xMax
-0.33852                yMin  [|y| < 1.2 d_i]
 0.33852                yMax
-0.5                    zMin  [read by 3D builds only]
 0.5                    zMax

#REFINEREGION
0                       iLev
+layer                  regions

#GRIDEFFICIENCY
1.0                     gridEfficiency

#CONSTANTPPV
F                       isPPVconstant   (per-cell particle count; PC static AMR)

#STOP
-1                      MaxIter
0.15                    TimeMax  [30 steps]

